Core Inheritance Principles
​The "IS-A" Test for Inheritance:
  
​The test for inheritance is the words "IS A". A lathe is a machine, so Lathe(Machine) is right.
  
​A lathe has a chuck — that is not inheritance, that's an attribute holding another object.
  
​Get this test wrong and you build family trees that make no sense: a Press is not a kind of Lathe, however similar their code looks.
  
​Why super().__init__(tag) Comes First:
The shared parts of the machine must exist before you bolt anything on. Skip that line and your lathe has no tag, no running flag, and no hours — a variant built on a drawing that was never issued. Every child's __init__ starts by calling its parent's.
